LICENSING - one project, four zones  (canon: docs/00_01 §8)
================================================================================

SilkenNet is released under a mission-driven, DEFENSIVE-PUBLICATION-FIRST IP
posture. We do NOT seek patents on this work; we publish it so it stays free for
all forests and cannot be captured by anyone.

  CODE      backend (Rails) / firmware (C) / tooling (Py, C#) / IaC (HCL, TS)
            .. GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later (per-file SPDX)        -> ./LICENSE
  CONTRACTS Solidity smart-contracts (contracts/*.sol)
            ... MIT (per-file SPDX; on-chain composability / audit-tooling /
            OpenZeppelin-consistency; ratified DOC-T.47)  -> SPDX headers
  HARDWARE  gyroid anchor / EBFC / PCB design (sources in docs/01_*, docs/02_*
            and any future CAD/gerbers) ... CERN-OHL-S-2.0 -> ./LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt
  DOCS      SSOT documentation (docs/**) ... CC-BY-SA-4.0   -> ./LICENSE-DOCS.txt

Where a single file expresses a hardware design, that design is offered under
CERN-OHL-S-2.0 even if the surrounding prose is CC-BY-SA-4.0.

Every in-scope source file carries its own SPDX-License-Identifier line; the
zone map above stays the authority, and the per-file tags mirror it so that a
licence scanner reaches the same answer without reading this file. Several
classes of file are deliberately left untagged — together a few hundred of them,
so absence of a tag is never evidence of absence of a licence. The reason for
each exclusion is recorded in the header of scripts/spdx_headers.rb, which is
the authoritative list; the classes are, in brief: data a generator re-renders
(locale YAML, schema dumps, lock files), formats with no comment syntax (JSON),
templates that emit into rendered output (ERB), documentation (covered by
LICENSE-DOCS.txt), generated binstubs, tool config — and files carrying a
THIRD PARTY's copyright.

On that last class we make no licence claim at all: the upstream notice inside
each file governs. Those files, and the vendored submodules and packages they
come from, are inventoried in ./THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.

